BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jejune w/ Ethel Meserve
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260712T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260712T230000
UID:27e1686856ec6331c88a7e7ff1153954@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:The San Diego via Boston alt trio that disappeared before most
  folks caught on. Jejune\, formed at Berklee College of Music in 1996 and 
 relocating to San Diego\, spent years building a sound that owed as much t
 o dream pop as it did to the emo scene they were part of. Male-female dual
  vocals\, guitars that shifted from jangly to blown-out\, songs that hit h
 arder than anything around them at the time. Putting out two genre-definin
 g records on Big Wheel Recreation\, Junk and This Afternoon's Malady\, a s
 plit with Jimmy Eat World\, and then abruptly breaking up in the year 2000
 \, leaving the world to catch up. The world did. The records lived on in r
 ecord collections and passed between fans like a secret worth keeping — 
 and a younger generation found them just as hungry for it as anyone who wa
 s there the first time around. Now\, after a successful run through Japan 
 on the Sakura Nights tour and some excellent record reissues courtesy of T
 he Numero Group\, the emo indie rockers are back and touring the U.S. for 
 the first time in over twenty-five years. All three original members. All 
 the songs. No excuses to miss it.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/dk2e7g-jejune-w-ethel-meserve-12th-jul-songbyrd-
 washington-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Living Space Live ft. Funsho
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260718T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260718T230000
UID:f4eece7b15904e6a2d048789c7e0d5f2@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:The Living Space ft. Funsho with Hameed Idowu\, Tony Thames & 
 Aden Simone Funsho is a singer\, songwriter\, and producer blending altern
 ative R&B with Afro‑inspired rhythms rooted in his Nigerian heritage. Af
 ter earning national recognition on NBC’s The Voice (Season 15)\, with p
 raise from Jennifer Hudson\, Kelly Clarkson\, and Mariah Carey\, he has co
 ntinued to carve out a lane defined by rich tone\, emotional depth\, and g
 enre‑bending creativity. Fresh off his LP From the Mind of Man\, Funsho 
 now channels his vision into The Living Space\, a concert series he create
 d to spotlight bold artistry and emerging talent. Each installment pushes 
 the boundaries of contemporary sound and offers an intimate\, immersive ex
 perience for listeners who crave music with soul\, intention\, and edge. \
 \*\\*\\* Hameed Idowu\, a Nigerian-American singer\, rapper and songwriter
 \, is redefining music by blending the vibrant rhythms of Afrobeats with m
 odern alternative trap and pop. Born in Nigeria and relocating to the DMV 
 (D.C.\, Maryland\, Virginia) area 20 years ago\, Hameed sees music and lif
 e as inseparable. His experiences spanning the challenges of his Nigerian 
 roots\, the perceived glamour of a musician’s life in the U.S.\, and the
  emotional rollercoaster of relationships fuel his creative output. “I w
 ant my music to inspire and touch someone the way music moves me\,” he s
 ays. As a pioneer in merging Afrobeats with trap and pop\, Hameed has dive
 rsified the American music scene with his viral 2016 single Wazy and a cat
 alog of five EPs. His projects Metanoia I & II explore transforming mindse
 ts for the better\, while Middle Ground reflects the tension of navigating
  dual cultures and striving for success. His Before I Dive In series\, inc
 luding the 2024 release BIDII\, delves into letting go of burdens\, friend
 s\, habits\, or grudges to embrace his destined path. The final chapter of
  this trilogy\, slated for 2026\, may mark his last EP unless major and or
  industry support propels him forward. Drawing inspiration from icons like
  Sunny Ade\, 2Face\, Michael Jackson\, Kanye West\, Drake\, and Meek Mill 
 and many more Hameed views music as a universal language capable of unitin
 g people across divides. While promoting BIDII\, he’s crafting his next 
 release but remains candid about his future. Without significant backing\,
  he may redirect his energy from music projects to other avenues of positi
 ve impact\, though his love for creating music will endure through singles
 . Hameed’s mission is clear. Use his art to bring people together and mo
 ve the world toward a better place. With his unique sound and heartfelt st
 orytelling\, he’s a rising force in music’s evolving landscape. \\*\\*
 \\* Tony Thames is a producer/singer-songwriter from Brooklyn\, NY. Raised
  in a colorful and eclectic Caribbean family\, his music is a patchwork of
  experiences and inspirations ranging from Prince and Pharrell to Bob Marl
 ey and Joni Mitchell. \\*\\*\\* Aden Simone is an alternative R&B artist w
 hose sound blends soulful warmth\, atmospheric production\, and emotionall
 y sharp storytelling. Influenced by voices like Donnell Jones\, Miguel\, S
 ZA\, and Solange\, she crafts music that feels intimate\, textured\, and d
 eeply human. Her debut EP Nightpill introduced her lush harmonic style\, a
 nd she has continued to build momentum with standout singles\, collaborati
 ons\, and creative visual content. Recognized by artists like Raheem DeVau
 ghn and supported by tastemakers including Miss Milan\, Aden brings a dist
 inct perspective shaped by her neurodivergent creative process\, offering 
 listeners a world that is honest\, immersive\, and impossible to forget.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/2w6nb6-the-living-space-live-ft-funsho-18th-jul-
 songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sabel Jane
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260701T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260701T230000
UID:729586bde46991968c52b7b2e247df77@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:SABEL JANE is the new solo project of D.C.-based artist Izzy B
 urke. Most known for her work with celebrated rock acts Cherub Tree\, Mode
 st Goddess\, Roscoe Tripp\, and Venray\, as well as dream-pop duo Letters 
 to Delphi\, Burke is now stripping away the noise to highlight her incisiv
 e lyricism\, evocative vocals\, and ear for understated yet compelling com
 positions. Blending intimate singer-songwriter lyricism and a lofi-folk ae
 sthetic with the unabashed intensity of 90s female-fronted indie rock\, Sa
 bel Jane is her offering to those who crave the cutting\, alt rock edge of
  PJ Harvey alongside the consolatory tenderness of Adrianne Lenker\; to th
 e ones who seek out both the emotional rawness of Elliott Smith and the po
 etic abstractions of Patti Smith\; and to listeners who can appreciate the
  weight of silence as much as that of sound. \\*\\*\\* XK Scenario is a Pu
 nk/Prog/Hip-Hop/Jazz band based out of Falls Church\, VA led by vocalist K
 aleab Elias and guitarist Alex Menick. They have over a decade of experien
 ce playing/performing music. They have shared stages with Flobots\, Scream
 \, Soulside\, The Messthetics\, and Ian MacKaye. They combine technical an
 d cerebral music with simple and emotional performances\, once described a
 s "Rage Against The Machine on bath salts." The lyrics crafted by lead voc
 alist Kaleab are born from a lifetime of voracious reading and confrontati
 on with the hardships of life. If you want art that isn't made to appease 
 people or algorithms\, but is instead made from a hunger for self-expressi
 on\, and connection towards others. Then XK is the band you've been search
 ing for. \\*\\*\\* Grace A. Keller is a Washington\, DC based singer-songw
 riter whose music lives in the space between longing and self-discovery. S
 he is also the frontwoman of the indie rock band Hotel Sewing Kit. Her sol
 o work is rooted in emotional honesty\, combining reflective lyricism\, de
 licate guitar\, and a tender vocal style inspired by artists like Adrianne
  Lenker\, Elliott Smith\, and Tracey Thorn.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/g5xddb-sabel-jane-1st-jul-songbyrd-washington-dc
 -tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mayonnaise w/ Black Wolf & The Thief\, Vivian Grey
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260719T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260719T230000
UID:e5b7a7328e4fba8b3a207ce663eec273@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:Mayonnaise\, based in Washington\, DC\, combines frenetic lyri
 cs\, Indie sleaze guitars\, and emo-adjacent beats for a unique\, all-orig
 inal sound. Inspired by early 2000s indie classics that continue to hit tw
 o decades later\, Mayonnaise is the secret ingredient for your sonic sandw
 ich. \\*\\*\\* From the heart of Warren\, OH\, Black Wolf & the Thief brin
 gs a genre-bending storm of sound that's part soul\, part rock\, part groo
 ve and 100% original. With Carolyn's powerhouse vocals and poetic lyricism
  riding the wave of Clay's jazz-infused\, aggressive piano\, this duo crea
 tes a fusion like no other. Think the raw energy of The Doors and Jefferso
 n Airplane meets the modern textures of Glass Animals and Bon Iver\, all w
 rapped in the smooth vibes of Leon Bridges and Alicia Keys. Over the past 
 decade\, they've electrified more than 25 venues across NE Ohio\, Western 
 PA\, and Western NY\, including stages at Federal Frenzy (Youngstown)\, Mi
 llvale Music Festival (Pittsburgh)\, and Highland Square PorchRokr (Akron)
 . If you haven't experienced their live show yet\, now's the time. \\*\\*\
 \* Vivian Grey is a trans singer-songwriter\, producer\, and music educato
 r creating sad queer music for other sad queer people. Her songs are intim
 ate expressions of her proudly trans experience in all of its forms - love
 \, trauma\, sacrifice\, and a quiet\, stubborn hope. She aspires to create
  the saddest song ever written.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/avq3md-mayonnaise-w-black-wolf-the-thief-vivian-
 grey-19th-jul-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cola
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260716T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260716T230000
UID:116f15a34f4fc294b9c69f91f57f17fc@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:C.O.L.A. is sort of a self-titled album. It’s an acronym for
  Cost of Living Adjustment\, a fitting conceptual framework for the band
 ’s third record. Why? Because C.O.L.A. considers\, among other things\, 
 socialism vs. hell. It considers: rolling the dice of life. The eerie and 
 sweet pangs that nostalgia can provoke. This is not new territory for band
  members Tim Darcy\, Evan Cartwright\, and Ben Stidworthy. It is\, in Cart
 wright’s words “a deepening of what we’ve been doing.” C.O.L.A. is
  an intricate\, beautiful\, and sometimes strange record. It is the band
 ’s most refined offering. A perfection of carefully honed aesthetic impu
 lses. Cola\, as a band\, says Darcy is defined by its “tasteful minimali
 sm.” A deep appreciation for making music that is romantic\, subtle\, an
 d deceptively intense. C.O.L.A.\, however\, is the band’s most maximalis
 t work to date. This is a little tongue and cheek (“We were so worried\,
 ” says Cartwright\, “About all the songs on this record being too diff
 erent”). In practice\, this maximalism means that a song like “Hedgesi
 tting\,” has both live drums and a sample drum loop. “Hedgesitting\,
 ” is a gorgeous\, lush song. It’s like a deconstructed\, chopped & scr
 ewed b-side from the Cure’s Disintegration. It’s also a little indebte
 d to Sarah Records. “When you were young\,” Darcy sings at the song’
 s start\, “you came to make it.” C.O.L.A.\, like everything written by
  the band\, is inherently collaborative. The band writes everything separa
 tely\, then comes together and works in the studio. Look again to “Hedge
 setting\,” to see this in action\, which started out with chords that Da
 rcy had sent\, then the band expanded it together\, with Stidworthy remixi
 ng it right before heading to the studio. This division of labor works int
 uitively. It is a part of the band’s DNA to say\, take an arrangement St
 idworthy wrote\, and then have Darcy and Cartwright build upon it. Take 
 “Favoured Over the Ride\,” as an example. “I wanted to create a dusk
 y\, melancholy palette for Tim to write lyrics for\,” says Stidworthy. T
 he song starts with a lonely\, dreamy guitar riff. Then there’s a crisp 
 line of bass and it all comes into focus: “What’s on the ceiling that
 ’s caught your gaze?” sings Darcy. It’s a moment of clarity on a rec
 ord that is interested abstraction. C.O.L.A. is full of these clarifying m
 oments: where a whole swirl of feelings become so clear that it almost hur
 ts a little bit. \\*\\*\\* PORTRAiTS\, the debut full-length from Kentucky
 -based art-rockers PARKiNG\, captures this unforgiving sense of dread\, un
 ease\, and mania with haunting accuracy. Its sprawling and oftentimes poli
 tically charged sound is a perfect fit for the ledge\, for the cusp of col
 lapse\, and for the dreadful isolation of twenty-first-century America. Sp
 anning ten tracks and clocking in at nearly forty-five minutes\, ‘PORTRA
 iTS’ features pulsating post-punk explosions\, haunting orchestral abstr
 actions\, and fresh takes on the last half century of art and noise rock.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/avqlqv-cola-16th-jul-songbyrd-washington-dc-tick
 ets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ally Nicholas
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260614T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260614T223000
UID:5621f393a505bebca91cbc8a7cbff6eb@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:Up-and-comer Ally Nicholas is bound to make you a fan of rock 
 and all that the genre has to offer. Born in Chicago\, her journey has not
  been one without bumps in the road. Early adolescence proved to be tumult
 uous\, and Nicholas found no reprieve in her teenage years. Turning to mus
 ic for comfort\, songwriting quickly became the only way to make sense of 
 the world happening around her. Characterized by a seasoned\, innate darkn
 ess and drawing from subgenres like grunge\, indie and metal\, Ally soon f
 ound hope and direction in pursuing her artistry. After dropping out of co
 llege she found a home at a Manhattan-based studio\, Engine Room Audio. Fr
 om there she worked toward her goal of becoming a recording artist. With o
 nly a handful singles out\, Ally has amassed over twenty million streams a
 cross platforms and has received recognition by publications like One's To
  Watch and Euphoria Mag.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/py88rw-ally-nicholas-14th-jun-songbyrd-washingto
 n-dc-tickets
