DESCRIPTION:Adele Marie (she/her) is a classically-trained vocalist and so
 lo experimental folk artist based around DC. She performs introspective mu
 lti-instrumental looping sets & intimate acoustic songs. Expect layers of 
 prepared guitar noise and free-associative lyrics within nostalgic melodie
 s and punchy dynamic shifts (plus a cosmic disco egg and rainbow furby\, c
 ause why not?!) . After the show\, embrace your surreal alter ego with an 
 original blind contour line drawing by Adele Marie herself. \\*\\*\\* Wash
 ington DC cult sensations The Electric Grandmother\, the inventors of “S
 itcom-Core\,” are an apocalyptic pop duo who bring you comedic musical c
 haos wrapped in the shiny package of nostalgia\, filtered through the lens
  of America's sweethearts of the underground. \\*\\*\\* Yellow Velvet is a
  group of friends with a blended background of jazz\, classical\, and chor
 al training who have been making music in the DMV for over three years. Th
 ey play indie jazz with intricate time signatures\, lush harmonies\, and c
 harming doo-wop sensibilities. Brookelove Hanlon brings a lifetime of expe
 rtise on the bass\, Chris BD is just as comfortable playing a jazz club as
  he is in a Chopin competition\, and vocalists Pigeon Valentine and Connor
  Laughland have perfected the dual arts of harmonizing together and tastef
 ully coordinating outfits.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
